\chapter{Thermal Envelope Modeling}

\section{Heat Dissipation Model}

Thermal load $Q(t)$ is modeled as:
\[
Q(t) = \sum_{i=1}^{N_{\text{blocks}}} P_i(t),
\]
where $P_i(t)$ is instantaneous power consumption of block $i$.

Heat transfer through vapor chamber assembly:
\[
\Delta T =
\frac{Q(t)}{hA},
\]
with $h$ the heat transfer coefficient and $A$ the effective surface area.

