\chapter{Cloud \& Edge Infrastructure Architecture}

\section{Distributed Node Topology}

Nodes are deployed in a hierarchical mesh:
\[
\mathcal{N} =
\{\text{Edge}_i,\ \text{Regional}_j,\ \text{Core}_k\},
\]
with inter-node bandwidth:
\[
B_{ij} = \frac{S}{\tau},
\]
where $S$ is packet size and $\tau$ is propagation latency.

\section{High-Availability Scheduling}

Fault-tolerant scheduling uses:
\[
R(t) = e^{-\lambda t},
\]
with $\lambda$ the failure rate. Active-active clustering ensures:
\[
R_{\text{cluster}}(t) =
\prod_{i=1}^{M}
e^{-\lambda_i t}
\approx 0.99999.
\]

