\chapter{Security \& Cryptographic Enforcement}

\section{Zero-Knowledge Verification}

All hardware telemetry and configuration updates are validated using ZKPs:
\[
\text{Verify}(x) \rightarrow
\begin{cases}
\text{true}, & \text{if proof is valid},\\
\text{false}, & \text{otherwise}.
\end{cases}
\]

\section{Quantum-Resistant Lattice Encryption}

Communication channels use lattice-based encryption:
\[
c = \text{Enc}_{\text{lattice}}(m, k),
\]
where $m$ is message payload and $k$ is the public key.

\section{Tamper-Evident Audit Trails}

Audit logs are hashed:
\[
H = \text{SHA3}(D \parallel t \parallel \text{sig}),
\]
ensuring immutability across distributed nodes.

